├── GEN_BIT_OUT/                          Reports generated automatically by run.sh
├── RESULTS_PROOF/                        Waveform screenshots, timing/power/DRC reports,
├── Application/                          Firmware — main.c is ours, rest is unmodified
└── DVCon_SoC_SRC/
    ├── AS1061_SYSTEM/      VEGA processor — unmodified
    ├── MEMORY_IP/          ROM — our compiled firmware image is loaded here
    ├── TB/                 Testbench — unmodified
    ├── TOP/                Top.vhd — unmodified
    └── ACCELERATOR_IP/     >>> OUR ACCELERATOR <<<
        ├── Accelerator_Top.v
        ├── axi_master_interface.v
        ├── axi_slave_interface.v
        └── top2_comparator.v

======================================================================
HOW TO REPRODUCE OUR RESULTS
======================================================================

No files need to be edited. The firmware is already built and its
output (.mif) is already loaded into
DVCon_SoC_SRC/MEMORY_IP/rom_32KB_axi/, so simulation works
immediately.

1. RUN THE SIMULATION

   cd DVCon_2026/RUN
   ./run.sh

   Select Option 1 -> Vivado Simulation.

   Once Vivado opens, in the Tcl Console at the bottom, type:

      run 500 us

   The signals listed below are to be checked in the waveforms and attached in 
   RESULTS_PROOF/ (also shown in  Report.docx, Section 5):

      acc_m_axi_awaddr, acc_m_axi_wdata
         - accelerator's result write-back
         
      acc_s_axi_awaddr, acc_s_axi_wdata
         - CPU writing to accelerator registers
         
      confidence_0..4, primary_score, alternative_score
         - internal scoring signals

2. RUN SYNTHESIS

   cd DVCon_2026/RUN
   ./run.sh

   Select Option 2 -> FPGA Implementation -> Synthesis Only.

   This automatically generates report_utilization_summary.rpt and
   report_hierarchical_utilization_summary.rpt in GEN_BIT_OUT/.

   We have additionally generated the timing, power, and DRC reports.

   Copies of these reports are already included in RESULTS_PROOF/.

======================================================================
REBUILDING THE FIRMWARE (OPTIONAL - NOT REQUIRED)
======================================================================

The firmware is already compiled and its .mif is already in place.
If you would like to rebuild it from source anyway:

   cd DVCon_2026/Application
   ./sim_app_compile_and_mif.sh

This regenerates accelerator_test.mif. Copy it into the ROM's memory
folder:

   cp Application/dummy_firmware_accelarator_64_64_matrix_20000/build/accelerator_test.mif DVCon_SoC_SRC/MEMORY_IP/rom_32KB_axi/

======================================================================
REPORTS AND PROOF (RESULTS_PROOF/)
======================================================================

- report_timing_summary.rpt
- report_power.rpt
- report_drc.rpt
- Waveform screenshots for all 5 test cases

======================================================================
TOOLS USED
======================================================================

AMD Vivado 2026.1 (Simulator + Synthesis), targeting Digilent
Genesys 2. No tools outside the contest's permitted list were used.



    
